;; errors.corpus -- exception-handling gap corpus (pending). Every form
;; on this list currently DIVERGES between real Clojure 1.13.0-alpha6 and
;; mova; it is a ledger of failures, not aspirational syntax. One session.
;;
;; NOTE on what already CONFORMS (excluded here, not repeated): mova's
;; ex-data/ex-message/ex-cause work correctly (`ex-cause` as of W-ERR,
;; field2 -- this file used to list `(ex-message (ex-cause (ex-info
;; "outer" {} (ex-info "inner" {}))))` as its own first pending line, an
;; inconsistency with this very sentence's older claim that predates
;; `ex-cause` actually existing; that line now conforms and was promoted
;; to `tests/conformance/corpus/errors.corpus`); a `try`/`catch`/`finally`
;; whose declared catch CLASS happens to match the actually-thrown
;; error's category (ArithmeticException/ClassCastException/
;; IllegalArgumentException/IndexOutOfBoundsException/
;; NullPointerException/ExceptionInfo, each verified individually) gives
;; the SAME `:caught` result on both sides -- but only because mova's
;; `catch` ignores the declared class entirely and matches ANY thrown
;; error (see the MISMATCHED-class lines below, which is where that gap
;; actually becomes visible); `finally` correctly runs and does not
;; swallow a propagating error on both sides (also excluded).
;;
;; Headline finding #1 -- "any class catches anything": a catch clause
;; whose declared class does NOT match the real exception still catches
;; it in mova (returns the catch body's value) where Clojure rethrows
;; the real exception uncaught. Three independent (class, actual-error)
;; mismatches below all show the same pattern.
;;
;; Headline finding #2 -- a second `catch` clause is rejected outright by
;; mova's parser ("try: only one catch clause is supported"), so
;; multi-catch fall-through-to-the-matching-clause is entirely
;; unavailable, unlike the single-catch-mismatch case above which mova
;; silently mishandles instead of rejecting.
;;
;; Headline finding #3 (silent-wrongness) -- `:pre`/`:post` are BOTH
;; ignored by mova's `defn`, but not in the same way: `:pre`'s condition
;; is evaluated for its side effects and its (unused) value discarded --
;; the call quietly succeeds with the true return value instead of
;; raising AssertionError. `:post`'s condition uses the compiler-special
;; `%` binding for the return value, which mova's `defn` does not
;; implement at all, so `%` is an ordinary unresolved symbol AT CALL TIME
;; -- a different failure mode (loud, but for the wrong reason) than
;; `:pre`'s silent wrongness.
;;
;; Headline finding #4 -- STALE as of wave-C small sweep item 5: `assert`
;; (S6) and a best-effort `Throwable->map` (core.mova, single-exception
;; only -- no cause-chain walk, no real stack trace) now exist. Their
;; `assert`/`(Throwable->map (Exception. ...))` rows below are ERR-BOTH
;; (both sides now throw `AssertionError`, but the pending driver never
;; auto-promotes ERR-BOTH -- mova has no exception-class taxonomy to
;; prove the SAME thing was thrown, see this dir's own README); the two
;; `Throwable->map`-on-`ex-info` rows that DID start conforming (both
;; sides `OK`) were promoted to `tests/conformance/corpus/libstatics.
;; corpus`. `*assert*` still does not exist (still unresolved-symbol --
;; unmeasured by this task, not touched).
;;
;; Headline finding #5 -- `recur` misuse: wrong arity and recur-outside-
;; loop are BOTH caught immediately by mova (not a compile-time rejection
;; like Clojure, but also not a hang) -- see the `arity error`/`error`
;; lines. The THIRD case, `recur` used in non-tail position inside a
;; `loop`, is the one form in this whole pending corpus family that
;; HANGS mova forever (confirmed with a 6s timeout via a piped mova REPL
;; session; Clojure rejects it at compile time instead). Kept as the
;; LAST line of this file since nothing after it would ever run.
(instance? clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo (ex-info "m" {}))
(try (/ 1 0) (catch ClassCastException e :caught-wrong))
(try (nth [1 2 3] 10) (catch NullPointerException e :wrong2))
(try (inc nil) (catch ArithmeticException e :wrong3))
(assert (= 1 2))
(assert (= 1 2) "custom message")
(defn pre-check [x] {:pre [(pos? x)]} x)
(pre-check -1)
(defn post-check [x] {:post [(> % 0)]} x)
(post-check -5)
(loop [i 0 j 0] (recur i))
(recur 1)
(loop [i 0] (+ 1 (recur i)))
